--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This package does not vendor third-party source. It declares runtime
dependencies in `install/requirements.txt`, which are installed from PyPI and
remain under their own licences. The notable ones at recall time:

  * sqlite-vec            — vector search extension for SQLite
  * sentence-transformers — embedding model runtime
  * torch                 — tensor runtime (GPU optional)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
MODEL WEIGHTS — THE PERMISSIVE FLEET, AND THE ONE EXCEPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Embedding and reranking models are downloaded at first use from the Hugging Face
Hub, cached under `~/.cache/huggingface/hub/`, and are NOT redistributed here.
They carry their own licences, verified 2026-09-07 from the HuggingFace registry
API directly rather than from documentation:

  PERMISSIVE — usable in commercial and non-commercial work alike:
  * nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5              apache-2.0   768-dim, the CPU tier
  * Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B                   apache-2.0   1024-dim, the GPU tier
  * Qwen/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B                    apache-2.0   the default reranker
  * BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3                     apache-2.0   the fallback reranker
  * cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base           apache-2.0   belief-engine NLI
  * urchade/gliner_multi-v2.1                   apache-2.0   entity extraction
  * MoritzLaurer/deberta-v3-base-zeroshot-v2.0  MIT          zero-shot
  * SamLowe/roberta-base-go_emotions            MIT          affect

  The fleet is uniformly PERMISSIVE but NOT uniformly Apache: two entries are MIT.
  Apache-2.0 additionally carries an express patent grant that MIT does not; if
  that distinction matters to a contract, it is those two that need naming.

  NON-COMMERCIAL — NEVER A DEFAULT, opt-in only:
  * jinaai/jina-embeddings-v5-text-small        cc-by-nc-4.0

  `jina` is selectable with WIZARD_EMBED_MODEL=jina and the installer warns when
  it is. It is NOT reachable by the hardware heuristic: a GPU host resolves to
  `qwen`, a CPU host to `nomic` (install.sh, resolve_embed_model). Under the
  prevailing reading the VECTORS a cc-by-nc model produces are themselves
  encumbered, so a brain embedded with jina is not made shippable by swapping the
  model forward — it would have to be re-embedded.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
ON ATTRIBUTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This package is the personal work of its author and is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or the property of any employer or client of the author. No
organisation's credentials or data appear in it, and no organisation's name is
used as a default, an identifier, or a fixture in anything that runs.
`voidloom/tests/test_notice_claim_holds.py` re-derives this paragraph against
the tree on every run. The brain's *contents* — the memories — are never
packaged: this repository carries the machinery only, and `claude_memory.db`
is git-ignored by design.

Some schema fields and built-in labels carry names from the system's first
installation (for example `drew_approved`, or the brain-tier labels `milamber`
and `eddie`). They are identifiers, not data: renaming them would need a
migration on every existing brain, so they are kept and documented instead.
